<GuideLayout
  title="Nylon 66 vs Standard Nylon for Premium Activewear"
  type="FABRIC COMPARISON"
  description="Compare Nylon 66 and standard nylon for activewear by hand feel, durability, abrasion resistance, stretch recovery, cost and buyer fit."
>
  <p>Nylon is widely used in premium activewear because it can feel smooth, supportive and flexible. Some brands also evaluate Nylon 66 for higher durability expectations, especially in performance products that need strong abrasion resistance and long wear life.</p>

  <h2>Where Nylon 66 Can Help</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Performance leggings that need better abrasion resistance.</li>
    <li>Premium training sets where durability is a selling point.</li>
    <li>Products positioned above basic athleisure price points.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When Standard Nylon Is Enough</h2>
  <p>Standard nylon blends can still be excellent for yoga sets, everyday leggings and studio wear when the knit structure, spandex ratio and finishing process are well controlled.</p>

  <h2>Decision Framework</h2>
  <p>Choose Nylon 66 when the product story and retail price can support the material upgrade. Choose standard nylon when launch speed, color range, MOQ and cost efficiency matter more.</p>
</GuideLayout>
